0
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Timing (minutes)
// The times of one event.
//   Warning before start: Minutes before the start that the doors open and everyone is warned (1 to 59).
//   Waiting room: Minutes players wait inside before the fight starts.
//   Duration: Minutes the fight lasts.
//   Closing: Minutes after the fight before the event can start again.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~59]       [Number]     [Number]     [Number]
//  AlarmTime    StandTime    EventTime    CloseTime
//----------------------------------------------------------
    2            1            5            0
end

1
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Schedule
// When the event starts. An event may have several rows.
//   Year: The year when the event starts. * means every year.
//   Month: The month when the event starts. * means every month.
//   Day: The day of the month when the event starts. * means every day of the month.
//   Day of the week: -1 Every day | 1 Sunday | 2 Monday | 3 Tuesday | 4 Wednesday | 5 Thursday | 6 Friday | 7 Saturday
//   Hour: The hour when the event starts. * means every hour.
//   Minute: The minute when the event starts. * means every minute.
//   Second: The second when the event starts. * means every second.
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [*/1970~9999]    [*/1~12]    [*/1~31]    [*/1~7]      [*/0~23]    [*/0~59]    [*/0~59]
//  Year             Month       Day         DayOfWeek    Hour        Minute      Second
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    *                *           *           *            *           50          0
    *                *           *           *            14          5           0
    *                *           *           *            22          5           0
end

2
//---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Entry and Places
// What a player needs to enter and where the teams are placed.
//   How many: How many of the required item are taken from each player who enters. 0 asks for no item.
//   Required item: Required item (category x 512 + index).
//   Item level: Level the required item must have.
//   Event map: Map of the event.
//   Waiting room: Gate where players wait for the fight.
//   Blue team: Gate where the Blue team starts.
//   Red team: Gate where the Red team starts.
//   Team outfit: 1 changes the look of each player to his team color during the event.
//   Minimum level: The lowest level that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Maximum level: The highest level that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Minimum resets: The fewest resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Maximum resets: The most resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Minimum master resets: The fewest master resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Maximum master resets: The most master resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ReqItemCount    ReqItem    ReqItemLevel    Map    WaitingGate    BlueTeamGate    RedTeamGate    SetSkin    MinLevel    MaxLevel    MinReset    MaxReset    MinMasterReset    MaxMasterReset
//---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1               6159       0               1      17             17              17             1          50          *           *           *           *                 *
end


3
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Winner Reward
// Prize for every player of the winning team (nothing is given in a draw).
//   WCoin C: WCoin C given to each winner. 0 gives none.
//   WCoin P: WCoin P given to each winner. 0 gives none.
//   Goblin Points: Goblin Points given to each winner. 0 gives none.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]
//  WC               WP               GP
//----------------------------------------------------------
    10               0                0
end